0PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in\nColorado...\n\nRio Grande Near Del Norte affecting Rio Grande County.\n\n.High flows and flooding will continue along the Rio Grande through\nDel Norte.  The river levels will continue to fall but remain in\nminor flood stage this morning.\n\nFor the Upper Rio Grande River...including Del Norte,.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande  near Del Norte.\n\n* WHEN...Until this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 5.5 feet, Minor Flood. The Del Norte Riverwalk Trail\nfloods.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:17 AM MDT Saturday the stage was 5.6 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 6:17 AM MDT Saturday was 6.4 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage late\nthis morning and continue falling to 3.2 feet Wednesday evening.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 5.6\nfeet on 06/10/1980.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b7706cb96d83e86d90f0fd7cf1c8f6d13428213c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b7706cb96d83e86d90f0fd7cf1c8f6d13428213c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 10:44PM MDT until October 24 at 12:15PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues along the\nRio Grande river and downstream waterways.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Mineral County and Rio Grande County...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1215 PM MDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding will continue along the Rio Grande from above\nSouth Fork to Monte Vista through Saturday morning.  Several roads\nremain closed and housing areas evaacuated due to high water. While\nthe upper reaches of the Rio Grande from South Fork to Del Norte\nshould see steadily decreasing water levels, river levels will\ncontinue to rise between Del Norte to Monte Vista as the runoff\nflows downstream.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1032 PM MDT, local law enforcement reported flooding in the\nwarned area. Flooding is already occurring.\n- Highway 160 remains closed between South Fork and Wolf Creek\npass.  Please heed all road closuers.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMonte Vista, Del Norte and South Fork.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T12:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6ed6bf45cfd2c9b7e2914c85b381b2ff9ad5afc7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6ed6bf45cfd2c9b7e2914c85b381b2ff9ad5afc7.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T11:29:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 241129 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 529 AM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Focus for heavier rainfall shifts to the eastern plains today and Sunday. - Some accumulation snow possible across the higher peaks this afternoon through Sunday morning. - Cooler and wetter weather areawide this weekend, with gradual warming and drying for the up","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T06:45:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 240645 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1245 AM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-251300- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T06:38:0